{"text": "2076110657\n\nFrom: Samuel.Nelson\u00a2PMUSA.Philip-Morris,Com\nDate: 9 May 96\nSub ect: MARLBORO MENTHOL PACKINGS EXPIRATION DATE\nTo: \"Brumberg, Chip\" <Chip.Brumberg\u00aePMUSA. Philip-Morris.com>, \"Sealey, David\"\n<David.Sealey@PMUSA. Philip-Morris.Com>, \"Holland, Ton\" <Tom.liolland@PMUSA,Philip-Morris\n\u2018com>\n\n\u2018To: CBRUMBER--PMUSAHUB CHIP BRUMBERG \u2018THOLLAND--PMUSAHUB TOK HOLLAND\nDSBALEY --PMUSAHUB DAVID SEALEY\n\nFrom: Samuel Nelson\n\u2018Subject: MARLBORO MENTHOL PACKINGS EXPIRATION DATE\n\nUT has sent me a letter asking if it is okay for thom to change the\nexpiration date from 7 months to 10 months for the two Marlboro packings.\nUT says that after their study that they concluded that all JT menthol\npackings expiration dates could be changed to 10 months. (The non-menthol\npackings of Marlboro and JT's packings now have a 10 month expiration date\ncode.) ~\n\nPlease advise what the current rule-of-thumb is for the USA Marlboro menthol\npackings.Also, please let me know if you have a problen with what JT is\nrecommending. I have told JI that I do not have a problem as long as you do\nnot have a problem and that they review their study that determined this\nchanged with me",
"words": [
